From: Velle Sinclair <brncomputerhelp@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 09:07:37 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 59/61] fix(text): a script sets a text's font and alignment

A script can write a text layer's font, horizontalalign and
verticalalign (lib.sceneScript.d.ts, ITextLayer), and Wallpaper Engine
draws the next frame with them. These writes were ignored, as any name
a layer does not have is ignored.

A music widget mirrors its text container to put the title on the
side of the album cover that faces the screen, and turns the title
left-aligned so it starts there. Kept right-aligned, the title ended
where it should have started and drew behind the cover. A clock's
applyUserProperties sets the font and alignment the user picked, and
the clock kept the ones the scene saved, whatever the settings said.

The text now holds the three as properties a script sets and reads
them every frame. A new font loads a new face, and a new alignment
lays the lines out again.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TrYdVZ7ULsVD9WKX2Az4Mw
